# Binary assets — never run line-ending (LF/CRLF) conversion on these.
# Git's autocrlf heuristic guesses "binary" from a NUL byte in the first
# ~8000 bytes; a small, mostly-text-structured PDF like the resume can slip
# past that check and get silently corrupted on checkout. Being explicit
# here removes the guesswork for every binary type the repo actually has.
*.pdf binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.xlsx binary
*.xlsm binary
